Apple Touch ID: enrol only under a Unix account and finger, as the aurora
kernel's SEP interface v5 requires, and report the matched identity.

By Ryan Murray, from aurora-silicon/aurora-sep-userspace 12f26f61
(ae9e9323, 2026-10-31), libfprint/0004-aurora-refuse-unbound-enrollment.patch,
as carried by aurora-silicon/alarm-aurora libfprint-aurora. LGPL-2.1-or-later,
like libfprint. Adapted: this driver keeps the kernel UAPI as aurora-bio.h, so
SEP_BIO_* reads AURORA_BIO_* and sep_bio_* reads aurora_bio_*, and the
aurora-bio.h hunk brings that header to the v5 UAPI of aurora-silicon/linux
f70f1acd352 (enrolment account and finger, LIST_ENCLAVE, DELETE_ORPHAN,
PREPARE_ENROL). Needs aurora-touchid-v4-and-v5.patch on top to keep v4
kernels working.

Original description:

  aurora: admit only bound enrolments and report match identity

  Resolve the Unix account and finger before any SEP write, prepare the empty
  Linux owner context, then start enrolment under kernel persistence checks.
  Report the SEP identity when single verify or identify lacks the requested
  print. Avoid DATA_FULL, which makes fprintd garbage-collect another print.

  Assisted-by: LLM

